snelling@bnr.ca (Peter Snelling) writes:

>Q: Aside from eating a tengu, how can you get intrinsic teleport control?

>Hint #1: It's something you eat.
>Hint #2: Eating it gives you a 1/3 chance of getting the intrinsic.
>Hint #3: You've to polymorph into something.

>A: Eat a ring of teleport control!

>It's true! If you're polymorphed into a metalvore (eg: a rock mole),
>you can eat a ring of teleport control, and you have a 1/3 chance of
>gaining the intrinsic.  This only works for rings that are metal
>(eg: gold, iron, ..., not coral, not black onyx, ...), so if teleport
>control happens to be non-metal, it won't work. Once you return to 
>human form, you keep the intrinsic.

>This also works for other rings: conflict, regeneration, 
>polymorph control, levitation (yikes!), protection, ...


>-- 
>Peter Snelling

